  "current": {
    "schema": "rise.current.v2",
    "id": "rise-changes-week",
    "title": "What changed in RISE: 13–14 October",
    "theme": "cobalt",
    "origin": {
      "kind": "model",
      "name": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
      "provider": "Anthropic, via Claude Code"
    },
    "scenes": [
      {
        "id": "calm",
        "engine": "turrell"
      },
      {
        "id": "field",
        "engine": "attractor"
      },
      {
        "id": "pendulum",
        "engine": "harmonograph"
      }
    ],
    "beats": [
      {
        "say": "This is what changed in RISE this week. Almost all of it is RISE Live.",
        "scene": "calm"
      },
      {
        "say": "RISE Live's face, Sophia, now holds every visual in one of three frames: the inner eye, the outer shell, and the full frame. The visual chooses the frame, and Sophia no longer leaves the room while a reading speaks.",
        "scene": "field"
      },
      {
        "say": "A change of visual within a frame is one blink of the aperture. Under reduced motion, every change is instant and nothing blinks."
      },
      {
        "say": "The ask bar now sits at the foot of the room, above the instrument and any on-screen keyboard, with the spoken words above it. That was the owner's decision."
      },
      {
        "say": "In the full frame, a figure or a generated scene is now fitted clear of the ask bar and the words. Before, the demo's horizon figure put its own label under the progress line, clipped."
      },
      {
        "say": "And Live now draws the circle frames at the size they are shown, so the harmonograph is no longer soft on a phone."
      },
      {
        "say": "RISE Live also remembers the room. Each new question goes up with the earlier questions and what RISE said, so a follow-up such as: what did Einstein say about it? can be understood. It lives in the page's memory only; leaving the room or reloading forgets it."
      },
      {
        "say": "A follow-up fixed how that memory names scenes, so a picture is no longer counted twice, and an answer's scene keeps the name the answer gave it."
      },
      {
        "say": "During a reading, a reader who names one of RISE's own visuals now gets it at once, with no model call, and nothing is counted as usage."
      },
      {
        "say": "That visual now also reaches the screen at once, instead of waiting for the next phrase. On one measured run, the wait had been 12 seconds."
      },
      {
        "say": "Two visuals the owner kept from the Sophia design study became engine options. The attractor can be a swarm of seven hundred particles, and the harmonograph can be rotary, two pendulums turning opposite ways.",
        "scene": "pendulum"
      },
      {
        "hold": {
          "ms": 2500
        }
      },
      {
        "say": "The swarm was slow in the venue, at 4 to 16 frames a second. It now adds each tick to its trail in one draw, and the flash gate samples on the GPU."
      },
      {
        "say": "For the team: a browser test that failed from run to run was traced to a race. A choice panel opened while the page faded in was hidden when the question field took focus. Now it stays open."
      },
      {
        "say": "That is the week in RISE.",
        "scene": "calm"
      }
    ]
  },
